banking and insurance. Companies like Texas Instruments were on the rise. They didn't need barges to reach the outside world. They had an airport. In my considered judgment, the canalization of the river would probably make Dallas go the way of the other port cities with a polluted channel which Houston has, increase crime, and increase deterioration of the inner city.
